That's the opportunity. These are the topics where one shared message beats five separate ones.`,
      build(s) {
        s.headline("Three topics run through every unit.", { x: 0.75, y: 1.2, w: 9, h: 0.75, size: 38 });
        const cols = [...THEMES, ...OWN];
        const x0 = 4.75, dx = 0.98, y0 = 2.95, dy = 0.6;
        s.rect(x0 - 0.45, y0 - 0.95, 3 * dx - 0.08, UNITS.length * dy + 0.85, { fill: "soft" });
        cols.forEach((c, j) => s.label(c, { x: x0 + j * dx - 0.55, y: y0 - 0.72, w: 1.1, align: "center", size: 14, tracking: 0.5, color: j < 3 ? "ink" : "muted" }));
        UNITS.forEach((u, i) => {
          const y = y0 + i * dy;
          s.text(0.75, y - 0.22, 3.4, 0.44, u, { font: "cond", size: 20, valign: "middle" });
          cols.forEach((c, j) => {
            const x = x0 + j * dx;
            if (j < 3) s.circle(x, y + 0.02, 0.15, { fill: "accent" });
            else if (j - 3 === i) s.circle(x, y + 0.02, 0.15, { fill: "muted" });
            else s.circle(x, y + 0.02, 0.15, { line: "rule", lineW: 1.25 });
          });
        });
        s.text(0.75, 6.2, 6, 0.32, "Illustrative map, not a survey.", { font: "light", size: 13, color: "muted", valign: "bottom" });
        s.source("Themes from our EAI proposal", { x: 6.58, y: 6.2, w: 6.0, align: "right", refs: ["eai"] });
      },
    },
    {
      role: "application", time: 65,
      notes: `So here's the move, and it fits inside what we already do.

Each semester, pick one owner per theme. Sleep might sit with Applied Performance, stress with mental health, time with academics.

That owner drafts two or three plain messages with input from the others. Short enough to fit on a locker-room card.

Then every unit says those same messages in its own setting: the weight room, the training room, the dining hall, the study hall. Athletes hear one story five times instead of five stories once. And for stress in particular: anything that sounds clinical goes straight to our licensed mental health staff.`,
      build(s) {
        s.headline("One message per theme. Every unit repeats it.", { x: 0.75, y: 1.2, w: 11.5, h: 0.9, size: 44 });
        const lines = [
          "Pick one owner for each theme every semester.",
          "Agree on two or three plain messages.",
          "Every unit says them in its own setting.",
        ];
        lines.forEach((t, i) => s.text(0.75, 2.75 + i * 1.05, 11, 0.7, t, { font: "light", size: 30, lineH: 1.1 }));
        s.cite("eai");
      },
    },
    {
      role: "takeaway", time: 45,
      notes: `The line to keep: one message, many voices. Each unit keeps its own expertise and its own setting; on these three topics we just agree on the words.

Question for the room: which theme would we align on first, sleep, stress or time? Take a quick vote. Whichever wins becomes the pilot for next semester.`,
      build(s) {
        s.headline("One message, many voices.", { x: 0.75, y: 1.35, w: 11.5, h: 1.75, size: 96 });
        s.lead("Sleep, stress and time are already everyone’s topic. Let’s say the same thing.", { x: 0.75, y: 3.3, w: 9.2, h: 1.3, size: 24 });
        s.line(0.75, 4.95, 1.75, 4.95, { color: "accent", w: 3 });
        s.text(0.75, 5.15, 11.8, 1.0, "Which theme would we align on first: sleep, stress or time?", { font: "medium", size: 28, color: "accent", lineH: 1.15 });
      },
    },
  ],
};

